    "How to join",
    "Contact",
    "submit a project",
    "Handling donations and grants can be one of the hardest parts of running an open source project. OSE offers fiscal hosting: a simple way to receive funds, stay compliant, and share resources transparently — without creating a legal entity. That way, your project stays focused on code, not paperwork.",
    "// Key benefits",
    "Transparency by default: every donation, grant, or expense is public.",
    "Legal recognition across Europe: OSE gives your project a trusted fiscal home.",
    "Access to international funding: US foundations can donate with tax advantages thanks to ED certification.",
    "Fast onboarding: projects can be live and receiving funds within days.",
    "// How it works",
    "Fill out a quick form to submit your project and start the process easily.",
    "Launch your collective page with a public budget to show transparency.",
    "Accept contributions through credit card, PayPal, or bank transfer with ease.",
    "Reimburse contributors or pay providers, all tracked in real time openly.",
    "// faq",
    "Who can apply?",
    "Any open source project, regardless of size or maturity.",
    "Do we lose independence?",
    "No. Your project remains fully yours: your project, your rules.",
    "How long does it take to get started?",
    "Most projects are live within a week.",
    "Do you take ownership of the project?",
    "No. We never own or govern your project.",
